{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2021-02-05 21:54:00', 'title': 'PG&E TO DEPLOY NEW RISK MODELING AND FIRE SPREAD TECHNOLOGY TO FURTHER REDUCE WILDFIRE RISK', 'text': "SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--IN A PROPOSAL FILED TODAY WITH THE CALIFORNIA PUBLIC UTILITIES COMMISSION (CPUC), PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E OR THE UTILITY) DETAILED ITS ONGOING STRATEGY TO REDUCE WILDFIRE RISK, INCREASE SITUATIONAL AWARENESS, AND DEPLOY NEW TECHNOLOGY AND MODELS TO HELP KEEP CUSTOMERS AND COMMUNITIES SAFE. IMPROVEMENTS TO ITS 2021 PUBLIC SAFETY POWER SHUTOFF (PSPS) PROGRAM WERE ALSO PROPOSED. PG&E'S 2021 WILDFIRE MITIGATION PLAN (WMP) ENHANCES THE COMPANY'S"}